{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UXhUA6fKVd3Myx4meUzmDz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd076-b2sum\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/b2sum: Compute and Check BLAKE2 Message Digests\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS does not ship b2sum. Scripts that generate or verify BLAKE2 checksums using\n6\t  the GNU b2sum format must use the Homebrew reference binary. The Go implementation\n7\t  must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary (gb2sum, installed by coreutils)\n8\t  byte-for-byte on all flag combinations, using golang.org/x/crypto/blake2b, verified\n9\t  by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Compute BLAKE2b digests for one or more files or stdin and print them in GNU format, matching gb2sum behavior.\n13\t  - G2: Support --check (-c) to verify a checksum file and report mismatches.\n14\t  - G3: Support --binary (-b), --text (-t), --tag output format, and --length for variable digest length.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Digest computation\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: Must compute the BLAKE2b-512 digest of each named file and write one line per file in the format \"HASH  FILENAME\" (text mode) or \"HASH *FILENAME\" (binary mode). The default is text mode.\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: Must read from stdin and print \"HASH  -\" when no file arguments are given or when \"-\" is provided as a filename.\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: --tag must use BSD-style output format \"BLAKE2b (FILENAME) = HASH\". When --length is specified, the tag name must include the bit length (e.g., \"BLAKE2b-256\").\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: Must exit 1 when any named file cannot be opened, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Checksum verification (--check, -c)\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: \"--check FILE must read FILE, parse each line (GNU or BSD tag format), recompute the BLAKE2b digest, and compare to the stored hash.\"\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: 'Must print \"FILENAME: OK\" or \"FILENAME: FAILED\" for each entry. Must exit 1 if any check fails.'\n36\t      - R2.3:\n37\t          text: --warn prints a warning for each malformed line. --quiet suppresses OK lines. --status suppresses all output.\n38\t\n39\t  R3:\n40\t    title: Output format and digest length\n41\t    items:\n42\t      - R3.1:\n43\t          text: -b marks input as binary; output uses \"HASH *FILENAME\". -t (default) uses \"HASH  FILENAME\".\n44\t      - R3.2:\n45\t          text: --tag produces BSD tag format regardless of -b/-t.\n46\t      - R3.3:\n47\t          text: \"--length=N sets the digest length in bits. N must be a positive multiple of 8 and at most 512. Default is 512. Must exit 1 with an error message if N is invalid.\"\n48\t\n49\t  R4:\n50\t    title: Exit codes and SIGPIPE\n51\t    items:\n52\t      - R4.1:\n53\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed and all verified digests match.\n54\t      - R4.2:\n55\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be opened, any digest fails, or the checksum file is unreadable.\n56\t      - R4.3:\n57\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n58\t\n59\tnon_goals:\n60\t  - cmd/b2sum does not implement BLAKE2s; it computes BLAKE2b only.\n61\t  - cmd/b2sum does not implement keyed hashing or BLAKE2 MAC mode.\n62\t\n63\tpackage_contract:\n64\t  imports:\n65\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/hashutil\n66\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n67\t\n68\tacceptance_criteria:\n69\t  - id: AC1\n70\t    criterion: \"b2sum on a known file produces the correct BLAKE2b-512 hash in GNU format, matching gb2sum.\"\n71\t    traces:\n72\t      - R1.1\n73\t      - R1.2\n74\t      - R1.3\n75\t      - R1.4\n76\t  - id: AC2\n77\t    criterion: \"b2sum --check on a valid checksum file exits 0 and prints 'FILENAME: OK' for each entry.\"\n78\t    traces:\n79\t      - R1.4\n80\t      - R2.1\n81\t      - R2.2\n82\t      - R4.1\n83\t      - R4.2\n84\t      - R4.3\n85\t  - id: AC3\n86\t    criterion: \"b2sum --check on a file with a mismatch exits 1 and prints 'FILENAME: FAILED'.\"\n87\t    traces:\n88\t      - R1.4\n89\t      - R2.1\n90\t      - R2.2\n91\t      - R4.1\n92\t      - R4.2\n93\t      - R4.3\n94\t  - id: AC4\n95\t    criterion: \"b2sum --length=256 produces a 64-character hex digest, matching gb2sum --length=256.\"\n96\t    traces:\n97\t      - R3.3\n98\t  - id: AC5\n99\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gb2sum passes for all required test cases.\"\n100\t    traces:\n101\t      - R1.1\n102\t      - R1.2\n103\t      - R1.3\n104\t      - R1.4\n105\t  - id: AC6\n106\t    criterion: \"cmd/b2sum compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n107\t    traces:\n108\t      - R1.1\n109\t      - R1.2\n110\t      - R1.3\n111\t      - R1.4\n112\t      - R2.1\n113\t      - R2.2\n114\t      - R2.3\n115\t      - R3.1\n116\t      - R3.2\n117\t      - R3.3\n118\t      - R4.1\n119\t      - R4.2\n120\t      - R4.3\n121\t\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01FtosemCfHdah2LEnXSNxpq","session_id":"476fc32d-92d8-426e-a248-aa248daf431c","uuid":"3dc0de3b-9231-4095-9c67-e8bd917ccbc3","timestamp":"2026-05-23T01:44:41.639Z"}
